texture became sharper does not explain

216
00:18:13,523 --> 00:18:18,667
these geometric relationships. Emerging
into the bright exterior then brings distant

217
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:23,688
statues and buildings into one image. Both
nearby detail and a broad scene must be

218
00:18:23,688 --> 00:18:28,770
handled, but mesh selection, material
evaluation and lighting use separate budgets.

219
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:34,167
Nanite's 2020 reveal introduced a workflow
for selecting and supplying needed

220
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:38,819
detail from dense geometry. We
distinguish the 2021 technical description

221
00:18:38,819 --> 00:18:43,280
from later engine features. It does
not make unlimited triangles free.

222
00:18:43,573 --> 00:18:47,315
Geometry is partitioned into
clusters, grouped, simplified

223
00:18:47,315 --> 00:18:50,734
and repartitioned into
multiple representations. This

224
00:18:50,734 --> 00:18:54,733
supports finer-grained selection
than a few whole-object LODs.

225
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:58,748
The Nanite demonstration first
displays triangles and then switches to

226
00:18:58,748 --> 00:19:02,820
clusters. Distinguish the boundaries
of dense individual triangles from

227
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:06,892
those of larger colored groups. The
two modes present the same geometry

228
00:19:06,892 --> 00:19:10,964
at different organizational units.
Returning to the final material view

229
00:19:10,964 --> 00:19:15,036
also confirms that the debug colors
were not the actual surface colors.

230
00:19:15,036 --> 00:19:19,567
Observe the detail revealed by camera
movement and the source counters, without

231
00:19:19,567 --> 00:19:23,753
turning those counters into memory or
frame-time measurements made by us.

232
00:19:23,783 --> 00:19:29,085
The need for fine geometry depends on
projected error. The same world-space

233
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:35,023
deviation appears smaller at greater distance,
changing the required representation.

234
00:19:35,033 --> 00:19:39,521
Look closely at the sculpted face, then
view the whole building from farther away.

235
00:19:39,521 --> 00:19:44,228
Detail in the same world occupies different
image sizes at different camera distances.

236
00:19:44,228 --> 00:19:48,935
In the following diagram, we hold other
conditions fixed and double only the distance.

237
00:19:48,935 --> 00:19:53,149
Several conditions can change together
in the actual camera demonstration, so

238
00:19:53,149 --> 00:19:57,253
separate that observation from the
independent projected-error calculation.

239
00:19:57,283 --> 00:20:01,292
Our illustrative projection
estimate is focal length times

240
00:20:01,292 --> 00:20:05,647
world-space error divided by
distance. Doubling distance halves

241
00:20:05,647 --> 00:20:09,863
the estimate. This is not the
complete Nanite selection rule.

242
00:20:10,093 --> 00:20:16,386
Independently simplified neighbors can form
cracks. Group boundaries and repartitioning

243
00:20:16,386 --> 00:20:22,533
maintain consistency. Triangle reduction
alone does not solve hierarchy construction.

244
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:26,736
Selecting clusters and making their
data resident are different jobs.

245
00:20:26,736 --> 00:20:30,790
Rapid camera motion exposes both
visibility and streaming behavior;

246
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:34,300
triangle visualization alone
does not measure memory cost.

247
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:39,470
In the bicycle closeup, inspect the
thin tubing, wheel spokes and floor

248
00:20:39,470 --> 00:20:44,160
behind them together. Watch how
much screen area the small geometry

249
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:49,060
occupies and where other objects
hide it. Displaying complex geometry,

250
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:54,310
texture sharpness and reflected-light
quality involve different conditions.

251
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:59,280
Even when source counters appear,
one number cannot explain every cost.

252
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:04,460
Nanite is a geometry system, not a
lighting solution. We now connect it to

253
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:09,420
Lumen, which updates indirect illumination
and reflections over the scene.

254
00:21:10,443 --> 00:21:17,694
Lumen combines tracing methods with
cached lighting. We separate finding

255
00:21:17,694 --> 00:21:24,843
a hit, storing surface information
and querying the final illumination.

256
00:21:25,150 --> 00:21:29,725
Screen tracing uses detailed visible
surfaces. Misses or unsuitable

257
00:21:29,725 --> 00:21:33,890
screen-space paths can fall back
to scene tracing, preserving

258
00:21:33,890 --> 00:21:37,850
screen-space benefits without
relying on them exclusively.

259
00:21:38,203 --> 00:21:44,876
Software and hardware tracing can
use different scene representations.

260
00:21:44,876 --> 00:21:52,883
Distance-field and triangle-based modes
require explicit version and setting labels.

261
00:21:53,310 --> 00:21:57,513
The Surface Cache provides
reusable surface information at ray

262
00:21:57,513 --> 00:22:01,513
hits. Cards relate to capturing
meshes from multiple views;

263
00:22:01,513 --> 00:22:05,310
they are not simply replacements
for the original walls.

264
00:22:05,543 --> 00:22:11,443
Our cutaway separates walls, capture
cards and lighting caches in depth.

265
00:22:11,443 --> 00:22:16,523
Hit detection and cached-light
lookup receive distinct arrows.

266
00:22:16,807 --> 00:22:21,251
The reviewed initial UE5 reveal
includes Lumen off/on views showing

267
00:22:21,251 --> 00:22:25,629
changed indirect lighting in the
cave. Those pixels demonstrate an

268
00:22:25,629 --> 00:22:30,007
effect, not every internal pass
or a universal performance result.

269
00:22:30,290 --> 00:22:36,129
Nanite can accelerate mesh captures used by
lighting caches. That connection does not

270
00:22:36,129 --> 00:22:41,830
make it the definition of Lumen; geometry
supply supports a separate lighting task.

271
00:22:42,587 --> 00:22:47,364
A light change can affect direct
lighting and cached indirect

272
00:22:47,364 --> 00:22:52,063
lighting at different rates.
Partial updates require budgets

273
00:22:52,063 --> 00:22:56,527
and priorities, making cache
age a quality consideration.

274
00:22:56,633 --> 00:23:00,809
Now select a directional light in
the engine and examine the changes on

275
00:23:00,809 --> 00:23:05,102
walls and rocks. First identify the
lighting edit, then separate directly

276
00:23:05,102 --> 00:23:09,395
illuminated surfaces from surrounding
shaded ones. Intervals in which the

277
00:23:09,395 --> 00:23:13,923
presenter also moves the camera need to
be distinguished. We do not calculate

278
00:23:13,923 --> 00:23:18,333
an exact update time or brightness
ratio by simply joining different views.

279
00:23:18,733 --> 00:23:23,071
Newly exposed surfaces or major
lighting changes reduce history

280
00:23:23,071 --> 00:23:27,064
reliability. Stability and
responsiveness can conflict, so

281
00:23:27,064 --> 00:23:31,333
trails, noise and convergence
speed must be examined together.

282
00:23:31,623 --> 00:23:36,413
Cache coverage can fail on complex
surfaces or interiors. Debug views

283
00:23:36,413 --> 00:23:41,063
help identify missing coverage
before changing mesh organization or

284
00:23:41,063 --> 00:23:45,783
representation; brightness controls
alone cannot supply absent data.

285
00:23:45,983 --> 00:23:50,450
Thin walls and small bright
objects challenge representation

286
00:23:50,450 --> 00:23:54,620
resolution and sampling
budgets. A technology name alone

287
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:58,863
does not establish that leakage
or instability is solved.

288
00:23:59,157 --> 00:24:03,578
Separate fixed-camera lighting
changes from fixed-lighting camera

289
00:24:03,578 --> 00:24:07,659
movement. This distinguishes
screen-trace changes from scene

290
00:24:07,659 --> 00:24:11,877
updates, while exposure and
post-processing remain controlled.

291
00:24:11,883 --> 00:24:15,918
The next example is an interior with
windows. Inspect the region near the

292
00:24:15,918 --> 00:24:19,897
bright windows separately from the
wall behind the sofa and the ceiling.

293
00:24:19,897 --> 00:24:24,208
A bright window does not establish
sufficient indirect illumination throughout

294
00:24:24,208 --> 00:24:28,408
the room. Identify the darkening
transition and the bright state, then treat

295
00:24:28,408 --> 00:24:32,664
the following camera movement as a
separate observation. The source is not an

296
00:24:32,664 --> 00:24:36,975
exposure-locked measurement experiment.
It still provides a starting point for

297
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:41,451
distinguishing directly illuminated regions
from the other room surfaces. Connect

298
00:24:41,451 --> 00:24:45,983
the storage and update structure explained
earlier to this actual interior result.

299
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:51,774
Dynamic illumination does not imply
complete transport solved anew every frame.

300
00:24:51,774 --> 00:24:57,040
Lumen combines tracing, storage and
distributed updates as an engine system.

301
00:24:57,923 --> 00:25:02,669
We separated scene representations,
ray acceleration, sample reuse,

302
00:25:02,669 --> 00:25:08,053
geometry selection and lighting caches.
BVHs reduce intersection candidates,

303
00:25:08,053 --> 00:25:13,223
while probes and reservoirs manage
different forms of reused information.

304
00:25:13,497 --> 00:25:18,315
Nanite selects needed geometry; Lumen
traces and updates illumination.

305
00:25:18,315 --> 00:25:22,789
Sharing an engine does not make
their responsibilities identical.

306
00:25:22,789 --> 00:25:27,677
Evaluate information coverage, work
budget and update latency together.

307
00:25:28,010 --> 00:25:32,244
Next we connect shadow pages,
path tracing, reconstruction and

308
00:25:32,244 --> 00:25:36,478
post-processing. We distinguish
rendered frames from generated

309
00:25:36,478 --> 00:25:41,190
display frames and follow renderer
inputs and outputs through DLSS 5.
